   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "13 King's Parade (King's College Visitor Centre). Late-Victorian red brick front with Bath/Ketton-type stone quoin strips at both edges and stone window surrounds/mullions. Street-facing gable with fretted timber bargeboards and finial over the northern ~3.6 m (window triple); the southern ~1.5 m is plain brick under a bracketed eaves/corbel course (cornice_z = bracket line, gable apex rises above wall height). 1st and 2nd floors: triple of tall sashes in a stone frame, each standing on a bracketed stone ledge with iron railing (string_courses). Single sash in the gable. Ground: dark-grey fascia 'King's College Visitor Centre' with stone piers; dark entrance bay at the south end. Vertical scale fitted to walls.json height (photos suggest slightly taller storeys). Pane pattern not resolvable (assumed 1-over-1)."
